      "guidance": "Original integration guidance: Choose canvas playback for compact vector feedback when its renderer tradeoffs fit your browser targets. Bring separately licensed local animation data and a reviewed locally installed runtime; no .lottie, .wasm, native library, or playable animation is archived here. Disable autoplay and looping for reduced motion, retain an informative still state, and update playback when that preference changes. Destroy manually created players on teardown. The React adapter handles its own lifecycle and StrictMode reuse: do not blindly destroy its managed instance from another cleanup. Profile concurrent canvases and pause invisible motion.",
