      "examples": [
        {
          "code": "import Animated, { ReduceMotion, useAnimatedStyle, useSharedValue, withTiming } from 'react-native-reanimated';\nimport { Button, View } from 'react-native';\n\nexport function SlideFeedback() {\n  const offset = useSharedValue(0);\n  const style = useAnimatedStyle(() => ({ transform: [{ translateX: offset.value }] }));\n  return <View>\n    <Button title=\"Move indicator\" onPress={() => {\n      offset.value = withTiming(offset.value === 0 ? 24 : 0,\n        { duration: 180, reduceMotion: ReduceMotion.System });\n    }} />\n    <Animated.View accessibilityLabel=\"Position indicator\" style={[{ width: 20, height: 20, backgroundColor: '#174' }, style]} />\n  </View>;\n}",
          "description": "Original integration fragment; supply reviewed local dependencies, app state, and separately licensed animation data where required. Never execute archived text automatically.",
          "language": "tsx"
        }
      ],
      "guidance": "Original integration guidance: Use short timing transitions to connect a gesture or explicit state change to its visual result. The pinned README states Reanimated 4.x requires React Native's New Architecture and supported recent React Native versions; verify the exact compatibility matrix before adopting it. Pass ReduceMotion.System instead of overriding the user's accessibility preference. Keep persistent labels and a non-motion indication of state. Prefer transform/opacity work over expensive layout churn, avoid per-frame JS communication, and measure on a real low-end device. No native dependencies or worklet compiler output are included.",
