      "examples": [
        {
          "code": "function SlowSpin({ reducedMotion }: { reducedMotion: boolean }) {\n  const mesh = useRef<THREE.Mesh>(null!);\n  useFrame((_, delta) => {\n    if (!reducedMotion) mesh.current.rotation.y += Math.min(delta, 0.1) * 0.2;\n  });\n  return <mesh ref={mesh}><boxGeometry /><meshStandardMaterial /></mesh>;\n}\n// Surround with an HTML description; imports are from React, three, and @react-three/fiber.\n<Canvas frameloop={reducedMotion ? 'demand' : 'always'} dpr={[1, 1.5]}>\n  <ambientLight /><SlowSpin reducedMotion={reducedMotion} />\n</Canvas>",
          "description": "Original integration fragment; supply reviewed local dependencies, app state, and separately licensed animation data where required. Never execute archived text automatically.",
          "language": "tsx"
        }
      ],
      "guidance": "Original integration guidance: Reserve a 3D scene for spatial explanation, product inspection, or an intentional interactive accent rather than making every interface animate. useFrame subscribes a mutable callback to the renderer: mutate object refs, use frame delta, and avoid setState or fresh allocations each frame. Stop motion when reduced motion is requested and use demand rendering for a static scene; other interactive changes must invalidate that scene. Pause or unmount hidden canvases, cap device pixel ratio and scene complexity, and provide a meaningful HTML alternative to visual-only canvas content. Scope here is React in a browser, not a claim of universal renderer support.",
      "id": "github-motion-pmndrs--react-three-fiber",
      "license": "MIT",
      "license_path": "licenses/github-motion/pmndrs--react-three-fiber/LICENSE",
